course: dictionary
lesson: 7751
title: Punish: more than one meaning
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Punish usually means to make someone suffer or lose something because they did something wrong, so they learn not to do it again. Look at the words around it to be sure. «Getting a brother or sister punished for something they didn't do is one of the worst lies.» The clue is that the brother or sister did nothing wrong, so the punishment is unfair.
explain: Punish can also mean to treat something roughly. «The hot sun punished the plants» does not mean the sun was naughty. It means the heat was so strong that it harmed the plants. Try your meaning in the sentence: the hot sun made the plants suffer, and that makes sense.
explain: To check a meaning, swap your word in for punished and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning. «Blaming someone else for what you did hurts them twice: they get punished and they lose trust in you.» Punished here means made to suffer for a wrong, because the person did nothing wrong at all.
fact: Punish is a verb: punish, punishes, punished, punishing.
fact: «Punish» means to make someone suffer or lose something because they did something wrong, so they learn not to do it again.
fact: «Punish» can also mean to treat something roughly, as in «the hot sun punished the plants».
fact: «Punishing heat» means very hard heat, the kind that wears you out.
fact: Useful phrases are «punish someone for» something and «be punished».
exercise: «Blaming someone else for what you did hurts them twice: they get punished and they lose trust in you.» What does punished mean here? | Forgiven and thanked | Moved to a new seat | Given a prize for good work | *Made to suffer for doing wrong
exercise: «The hot sun punished the plants.» What does punished mean here? | *Treated roughly, so the plants suffered | Given new pots | Covered with a warm blanket | Watered gently
exercise: Which word is the past tense of punish? | punishing | punish | punishes | *punished
test: Mum says, «You will be punished for lying.» What does punished mean? | Given a treat | Praised loudly | *Made to suffer a consequence, so you learn not to lie again | Asked to tidy up
test: «Getting a brother or sister punished for something they didn't do is one of the worst lies.» Why is it so unfair? | *Because the punishment falls on someone who did nothing wrong | Because it is a true story | Because it is a joke | Because it makes a brother or sister happy
exam: In the story, «the villain is punished in the end.» What does punished mean? | Told to leave the village | Treated to a prize | *Made to suffer for the wrong they did | Forgiven and given a hug
